    8	## What was tested
    9	We view the binary prime indicator chi_P(n) for n in [1, 2^k] as a state vector
    10	in (C^2)^{otimes k} and measure its tensor-train (matrix-product-state) bond
    11	dimension at every bipartite cut. A polylog MPS would mean polylog-time exact
    12	computation of pi(N) and p(n). We compared against:
    13	  (i) a random binary vector at the same density,
    14	  (ii) the cumulative pi(n) (smooth),
    15	  (iii) the residual pi(n) - li(n) (oscillatory part).
    16	
    17	This is a NEW measurement for this project. Earlier work studied:
    18	  - product DFA states (`tensor_sieve.py`) — primorial blowup, different object;
    19	  - the divisibility matrix M[n, p] (`sieve_matrix_rank.py`) — different tensor;
    20	  - wavelet sparsity (`wavelet_*`) — single-mode basis, not multipartite.
