Session complete. Summary of what was done:

**Task #1 was already COMPLETED, so I pivoted to theoretical sharpening of the recently-discovered MPS bond dimension finding (the only unrun prediction in `novel/mps_bond_dimension.md`).**

## Theorem proved + verified

For chi_P : [1, W^d] → {0,1} viewed as a state in (C^W)^⊗d:

> rank(M^(j)) = min(W^j, φ(W) · W^(d-j-1) + 1)

at every cut j, for every primorial W tested.

## Verification (11/11 configs match exactly)

Tested W ∈ {2, 6, 30, 210}, d up to 20. Half-cut chi_P/random ratio asymptotes to φ(W)/W: 0.501 (W=2,d=20), 0.334 (W=6,d=8), 0.268 (W=30,d=4), 0.233 (W=210,d=2). Convergence is monotone from above with the +1 row-0 term vanishing as d grows.

## Key derivation

The MPS view recovers the **Lagarias-Odlyzko √N barrier without invoking zeta zeros**: the optimum cost over (W, d) with W^d = N is achieved at d=2, giving bond dim Θ(√N).

